        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): guard JSON.parse malformed input in parseJsonStringArray",
        "body": "fix(gateway): guard JSON.parse malformed input in parseJsonStringArray\n\n## Description\n\n`JSON.parse(trimmed)` throws an unhandled SyntaxError when the input is malformed JSON (e.g. truncated string, invalid syntax). This crashes the caller with a bare SyntaxError instead of a clear validation error.\n\n## Fix\n\nWrapped `JSON.parse` in try/catch to throw the same descriptive `Error` used for non-array or non-string element validation, so all malformed inputs produce the same message regardless of parse stage.\n\n## Test evidence (vitest, 16/16 passed)\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  16 passed (16)\n```\n\nIncludes 5 new focused regression tests for malformed JSON inputs:\n- ✓ throws descriptive error for malformed JSON instead of bare SyntaxError\n- ✓ throws descriptive error for truncated JSON\n- ✓ returns undefined for empty/undefined input\n- ✓ still validates non-array parsed values\n- ✓ returns parsed array for valid input\n\n## Real terminal evidence\n\n```\n=== fix(gateway): guard JSON.parse malformed input in parseJsonStringArray ===\nCommit: 03ff2fe6595\nDate:   2026-07-19T16:12:38Z\n\n=== Test suite (vitest, 16/16 passed) ===\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.10 /home/lizeyu/workspace/openclaw\n\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  16 passed (16)\n   Start at  00:13:44\n   Duration  2.73s (transform 1.06s, setup 227ms, import 1.94s, tests 437ms, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 6.71s\n```\n\n## Diff\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live-helpers.ts\n+++ b/src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live-helpers.ts\n@@ -141,7 +141,12 @@ export function parseJsonStringArray(name: string, raw?: string): string[] | und\n   if (!trimmed) {\n     return undefined;\n   }\n-  const parsed = JSON.parse(trimmed);\n+  let parsed: unknown;\n+  try {\n+    parsed = JSON.parse(trimmed);\n+  } catch {\n+    throw new Error(`${name} must be a JSON array of strings.`);\n+  }\n   if (!Array.isArray(parsed) || !parsed.every((entry) => typeof entry === \"string\")) {\n     throw new Error(`${name} must be a JSON array of strings.`);\n   }\n```",
        "branch": "fix/parse-json-string-array-guard",
